 the  people that perform the tests for the  licensure of the clinic itself and for  any subsequent testing so if the test is  considered waived which mean that it's  of the simplest complexity and appears  to be a exempt from a lot of the CLIA or  other related regulations be cautious  and look at that labeling because most  of those labels require that any  positive result be confirmed by a GCMs  or LC ms/ms type methods which could  lead to pretty expensive consequences if  the likelihood of positive results is  high which it usually is in chronic pain  patients so so it may not be appropriate  and I think I would caution you to look  at the details that are associated with  any test that's implemented in a clinic  setting before we're pursuing it and  subsequently billing for it  thank you dr. McMillan for your time and  for your presentation I would also like  to thank Lavery's for making today's  educational webcast possible before we  go I want to let everyone know that  today's webcast will be available for  on-demand viewing through February of  2018 you will receive an email from  lathers letting you know when this  webcast will be available for replay  please share that announcement with your  colleagues who may have missed today's  live event that's all for now thank you  for joining us and we hope to see you  again here soon at lab  goodbye
 

